# Append/prepend-only bookkeeping files: every branch adds its own entry at the
# same offset, so a three-way merge conflicts on content that never actually
# disagreed. Union-merge keeps both sides' entries instead of demanding a
# hand-resolution that always resolves to "take both".
#
# Union only engages where git would otherwise CONFLICT, so the question for
# each file is not "does it ever get edited in place" but "when two branches
# collide on the SAME lines, is keeping both the right answer, and is a wrong
# answer VISIBLE?" That is what the list below is selected on, and the second
# half of the test is the one that does the work — see the exclusions.
.prawduct/change-log.md merge=union

# DELIBERATELY NOT union-merged:
#
#   .prawduct/learnings.md + .prawduct/learnings-detail.md — these were added
#     here and then removed, because the visibility half of the test fails.
#     A union-duplicated `## ` heading is not merely cosmetic: `audit-learnings`
#     pairs the two files by EXACT title and `_take_active_narrative` breaks on
#     the FIRST match, so a retirement run cuts one block and silently orphans
#     the other — the failure its own docstring names ("cutting the wrong block
#     silently destroys an unrelated narrative"), against a file whose stated
#     invariant is never delete an entry. No doctor or janitor check pairs the
#     two files, so nothing would report the divergence. If such a check is
#     ever built, these two become safe to add — together, since union resolves
#     deterministically and giving it to only one could desynchronize the
#     ordering the index/detail pairing depends on.
#
#   .prawduct/operator-verification.md — entries flip PENDING -> PASSED in
#     place. A union resolution would leave one entry asserting both, silently,
#     in the file `/prawduct:pr` reads to decide whether live checks still
#     block a release. A conflict here should stop a human, not auto-resolve.
#
#   .prawduct/reflections.md — gitignored; it never merges at all.
#
#   .prawduct/project-state.yaml, .prawduct/backlog.md — structured records
#     edited in place, not append-only logs.
